  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: Eight trucks fight for a moving illuminated mountaintop control zone. One
    physically present, upright and grounded truck earns control seconds. Two or
    more opponents contest it and nobody scores; an overturned truck still physically
    contests while it remains in the ring. Distant compound colliders and airborne
    passes cannot award control. Default victory requires 60 cumulative uncontested
    seconds; choose 30 or 90 in setup. Every 40 seconds by default the hill relocates
    to an accessible connected plateau, with a three-second preview ring at the announced
    next site. Use the broad authored roads, bridges and ridges; shove rivals out
    using actual NWH collisions. Falling from a cliff costs recovery time. ACTION
    only recovers a genuinely stuck/overturned truck at a separated nearby safe plateau;
    it cannot warp a moving truck to the next hill. AI uses the existing LWS road
    planner and Fare Fight driving adapter, navigates the same roads, contests and
    physically rams; no hidden points. Shared arena/chase/full cab, free look, optional
    AI views, crew colors/names, shared weather and horn use collection controls.
    Match-end replay records actual movement and never changes the winner.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: be1034cebd9fa3643a48d11ef76e4708, type: 2}
